    "content": "# The Hermes Dispatch | August 27, 2026\n\n### 4 min read | TL;DR: NVIDIA drops a cheaper edge-AI brain for robots, Schwab adds three altcoins to its retail crypto desk, and spot Bitcoin ETFs have now sucked in $2.8 billion over eight straight days.\n\n---\n\n## The Rig\n\n**Agent TL;DR:** NVIDIA announced the Jetson Orin Nano 2, an entry-level edge-AI module that doubles inference performance while cutting power draw 40%, opening physical-AI projects to millions of developers.\n\nNVIDIA unveiled the Jetson Orin Nano 2 on August 25, a new robotics computer aimed at the bottom of its edge-AI stack. The module delivers 78 trillion operations per second of AI compute, an 8-core Arm CPU, and 8GB of memory, all in the same compact form factor as the prior Jetson Orin Nano Super. NVIDIA says it achieves roughly 2x the inference performance of the Super through better Tensor Cores and higher memory bandwidth. In 15-watt mode, it can match the Super's performance on about 9 watts, a 40% power savings. That matters for battery-powered drones, small robots, and vision systems that have to run real-time AI without a data center.\n\nThe new module runs NVIDIA's open robotics stack, Jetson AI Lab agent skills, and supports compressed LLMs and vision-language models such as Cosmos, Nemotron, Gemma 4, and Qwen 3. Early adopters named by NVIDIA include Cognex, Doosan Bobcat, Matic, and Wing, which is exploring it for delivery drones. NVIDIA says more than 3 million developers already build on its robotics stack. The module and developer kit are expected to ship in the first half of 2027, with pricing still unannounced.\n\n**Why it matters:** Physical AI is moving from prototype to product, and the cost of putting real-time perception, navigation, and interaction into small machines is about to drop sharply. Lower power and higher throughput at the entry tier means more founders can build AI hardware that does not need the cloud to think.\n\n**The play:** If you are building a robot, drone, or embedded vision project, start designing around the Jetson Orin Nano 2 toolchain now so you are ready when the 2027 kits land.\n\n**[Compare local LLM rigs →](https://hermesdispatch.dev/hardware/compare)**\n\n---\n\n## The Mine\n\n**Agent TL;DR:** U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs logged their eighth consecutive day of net inflows on August 26, pulling roughly $2.8 billion into the funds and pushing August above $3 billion, the strongest month of 2026.\n\nThe ETF bid came back hard. On Wednesday, U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs added about $232 million, according to SoSoValue, extending an inflow streak that began on August 17. The eight-day run has now drawn approximately $2.8 billion, and August inflows for the Bitcoin funds crossed $3 billion, roughly double April's total and already the strongest month of 2026. With three sessions left in August, another $160 million would make it the best inflow month since October 2025.\n\nBitcoin traded near $80,000 on Thursday, briefly touching an intraday high around $80,475, according to CoinGecko. The weekly ETF intake through August 21 was about $1.9 billion, the strongest since October 2025. IBIT has drawn $63.1 billion since launch, while GBTC has bled $27.6 billion over the same period.\n\n**Why it matters:** ETF inflows are the cleanest institutional demand signal in crypto. Eight straight days of buying, concentrated around the $80,000 price level, shows real money is returning after the mid-August outflow stretch.\n\n**The play:** If you are dollar-cost averaging, keep your schedule. If you are mining, lock in power contracts now before rising BTC price and ETF demand push difficulty and energy competition higher.\n\n**[Secure mining payouts with Ledger →](https://shop.ledger.com/?r=ca1b30139f19)**\n\n---\n\n## The Ledger\n\n**Agent TL;DR:** Charles Schwab announced it will add Solana, Avalanche, and Chainlink to Schwab Crypto in the coming months, expanding the platform beyond Bitcoin and Ethereum.\n\nSchwab Crypto, which launched in May 2026 with only Bitcoin and Ethereum, will soon support Solana, Avalanche, and Chainlink, the brokerage announced Thursday. The new tokens will join BTC and ETH as direct-trade options inside a separate crypto account linked to a client's Schwab brokerage account. Schwab said the additions are driven by client demand for established digital assets and noted it plans to keep expanding the lineup over time.\n\nTrades on Schwab Crypto are priced at 0.75% of the dollar value of each transaction. Schwab did not give a specific launch date and warned that it could delay, change, or withdraw support depending on market, regulatory, or operational conditions. The move comes as major brokerages and asset managers race to fold crypto into mainstream retail and advisory platforms.\n\n**Why it matters:** A $12 trillion brokerage adding altcoin spot trading validates SOL, AVAX, and LINK as investable assets for ordinary retail accounts, not just crypto-native exchanges. It also signals that TradFi firms believe crypto is now a sticky enough feature to keep clients from leaving.\n\n**The play:** If you have been waiting for a reputable broker to hold your altcoins alongside your stocks, this is your cue to compare Schwab Crypto's custody and fee structure against dedicated exchanges.\n\n**[Try TradingView free →](https://www.tradingview.com/?aff_id=167461)**\n\n---\n\n## Quick Bites\n\n- OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and more than 100 other companies issued a joint call for stronger defenses against rogue AI and advanced cyber threats.\n- Barret Zoph, co-founder of Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab, has left OpenAI and joined Google after a brief stint at the startup.\n- Google's AI Mode is expanding into travel, adding flight price tracking, hotel help, and booking assistance to turn search into an AI travel agent.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Mission Freedom: Behind the Scenes\n\n- **What we shipped:** The HermesDispatch newsletter pipeline is humming. Yesterday's issue, MF-20260826-001, went out to 1/1 subscribers via Resend and was published to the site at https://hermesdispatch.dev. The daily subscriber harvest and KV sync ran clean, and the last five issues from 2026-08-22 through 2026-08-26 all delivered successfully.\n- **Current experiment:** The Overnight Learning Orchestrator is now analyzing around 99 agent runs per night across 45 domains with a 0.0% failure rate, turning daily agent output into site and newsletter material faster.\n- **What's next:** The daily newsletter cron fires at 16:00 MDT today for issue MF-20260827-001, and the next deploy will push the newsletter to the website archive and update the issue index at https://hermesdispatch.dev.\n\n---\n\n*The Hermes Dispatch is written by dare404 from Boise, ID.*\n\n*Sources: NVIDIA newsroom, CoinDesk, SoSoValue, Charles Schwab press release, Yahoo Finance, Reuters, TechCrunch.*\n\n*Some links in this dispatch are affiliate or referral links. We may earn a commission if you click and buy or sign up. Your price doesn't change.*\n\n*Generated: 2026-08-27 15:45 MDT*"
